# Phase 7 checks for the chat and the change stamp (VS Code REST Client: click "Send Request" above a block).
# Start the API first (npm run dev:api) and load the sample data (npm run seed:api). The messages sent here
# stay in the database: run npm run seed:api again afterwards.
#
# The customer requests need a customer token and the admin requests an admin token: get them with the
# sign-in requests at the top of catalog.http, and paste them into @customerToken and @adminToken below.
# @thread is a conversation of that customer (GET /threads shows its id; the sample data uses th-0001 … th-0005).
# Errors come back as { code, message, meta }.

@api = http://localhost:4000/api
@customerToken = paste-a-customer-token
@adminToken = paste-an-admin-token
@thread = th-0001

### ---------------------------------------------------------------- Customer

### The customer's conversation (none or one): last message, unread count for the customer, updatedAt
GET {{api}}/threads
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### Start the customer's conversation (the portal asks only when the list above is empty) -> { id }
POST {{api}}/threads
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### The conversation with every message, oldest first, each with eventName. Another customer's: 404 NOT_FOUND
GET {{api}}/threads/{{thread}}
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### Mark the admin's messages as read -> { ok: true } ({ ok: false } for a conversation that is not theirs)
POST {{api}}/threads/{{thread}}/read
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### Send a message -> 201 with the message. The sender's name is the account's (a senderName sent here is ignored).
### Empty: 400 "Write a message first."; over 2,000 characters: 400; a ref that is not one of their reservations: 404
POST {{api}}/threads/{{thread}}/messages
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "body": "Hello po, can we add a cake table?", "ref": null }

### ---------------------------------------------------------------- Admin

### Every conversation, most recently active first (unread = the customer's messages the admin has not read)
GET {{api}}/admin/threads
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### One customer's conversation (the chat buttons on the reservation and customer pages look it up first)
GET {{api}}/admin/threads?customerId=cus-009
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### Start a customer's conversation -> { id }. An unknown customer: 404 "Customer not found."
POST {{api}}/admin/threads
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "customerId": "cus-004" }

### One conversation in full
GET {{api}}/admin/threads/{{thread}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### Mark the customer's messages as read -> { ok: true }
POST {{api}}/admin/threads/{{thread}}/read
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### Reply as the signed-in admin -> 201 with the message
POST {{api}}/admin/threads/{{thread}}/messages
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "body": "Yes, we can add one cake table." }

### ---------------------------------------------------------------- Change stamp

### { stamp }: moves by one after every write that succeeds; both portals ask every 15 seconds while visible
GET {{api}}/changes
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
